How It Works
Encryption: The flag is hidden in the encryptedFlag variable as a string of non-ASCII characters. 
Decryption Logic: The script iterates through each character of the encrypted string. It subtracts the ASCII value of the corresponding character in the key "picoctf" (repeating the key as needed) from the encrypted character's ASCII value. 
Modulo Arithmetic: The + 256) % 256 ensures the result wraps around correctly within the standard byte range (0-255), handling any negative values resulting from the subtraction. 
